  "plain_verdict": "BOTH MODEL ARCHITECTURE AND THE 512-TOKEN WINDOW DEFINE THE BOTTLENECK: DeBERTa-v3-base demonstrates markedly superior contextual discrimination on out-of-domain prompt injection (Deepset AUROC 0.8997 vs DistilBERT 0.9592, Deepset Recall 36.7% vs 73.3%), and significantly higher padding resilience at 2-5 sentences (DeBERTa 81.5% vs DistilBERT 28.5%). However, beyond 20-50 sentences, both transformer models face severe token dilution and the hard 512-token truncation horizon. Full retraining from scratch of microsoft/deberta-v3-base was NOT RUN (benchmarked at ~35s/step on CPU = 4.94 hours), but the pre-trained DeBERTa comparison confirms that model capacity provides substantial representation gains, yet context window chunking/sliding is mandatory for long documents."
